<div id="2026-09-05-helpdesk-ticket-staff-controls-and-stability" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-05 — HelpDesk: Todo creation stability, customer email visibility, and per-ticket email disable</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Fixed fatal "Can't locate object method 'project_code'" when staff used Work On / Escalate on tickets. Made the Todo creation robust with all required fields and a site-aware project lookup. Added staff-only display of the ticket holder's email address + direct mailto: reply link. Added a per-ticket "Disable emails" / "Enable emails" toggle (stored in metadata) so spam or unwanted tickets generate no customer notifications at all. Ensured todo creation never auto-sends email to guests (internal system message only). Changed internal todo messages to sender_type 'system'.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The original create_todo/escalate_ticket implementation made incorrect assumptions about the SupportTicket model and produced incomplete Todo rows (missing parent_todo, due_date, project_id, last_mod_*, etc.). Staff needed to see the customer's email and have a kill-switch for notifications on spam tickets without losing the ticket thread.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/HelpDesk.pm</code> (create_todo, escalate_ticket, toggle_customer_emails, view_ticket, email send guards), <code>Comserv/root/CSC/HelpDesk/ticket_view.tt</code> (staff email display + toggle buttons), new changelog entry.</p>
</div>